# Allowlist, not denylist. Claude Code writes credentials, session transcripts,
# and new state directories into this folder as it updates. Ignoring everything
# by default means a new state dir fails closed (unsynced) rather than open
# (published). Add new config here deliberately.

*

# --- Portable config: the stuff worth having on every machine ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!settings.json

!skills/
!skills/**
!commands/
!commands/**
!agents/
!agents/**
!workflows/
!workflows/**
!hooks/
!hooks/**

!board_extension/
!board_extension/**
# Built output and deps rebuild from source on each machine.
board_extension/node_modules/
board_extension/out/

# Installed by the twg CLI's own setup, not authored here. Each machine gets
# its own copy when it runs `twg setup`, so syncing them would fight the
# installer. Delete them with `rm -rf ~/.claude/skills/twg*` if unwanted.
skills/twg/
skills/twg-*/

# --- Deliberately NOT synced, even though they sit next to the above ---
# .credentials.json   OAuth token
# .claude.json        (parent dir) user id, machine id, prompt history, MCP keys
# settings.local.json machine-local permission grants
# projects/           full session transcripts (~276MB)
# file-history/       snapshots of every file edited (~102MB)
# plugins/            cloned marketplaces; re-fetched on demand
# history.jsonl       your prompt history
# backups/ cache/ sessions/ shell-snapshots/ session-env/ paste-cache/
# tasks/ plans/ jobs/ daemon/ ide/ chrome/ downloads/ statsig/
